trait-language-terraslavic-name = Terra Slavic
trait-language-terraslavic-desc =
    A long split dialect of Sol Common, sounding like a mixture of Russian and Mandarin Chinese.
    Over the years, it has turned into the language of many Sol residents and space drifters.
    To an outsider it sounds similar, but compared to Sol Common it sounds like gibberish.

trait-language-tau-name = Tau
trait-language-tau-desc =
    A language spoken across the Tau System, hence the name.
    Most notably, it is the official language of the Imperial Coalition of Tau; spoken by nearly all people in Coalition territories.
    It is notoriously difficult to learn for outsiders due to its lack of tone and untraditional vowel system.

trait-language-triadian-name = Triadian
trait-language-triadian-desc =
    Due to the overwhelming amount of Tau speakers in the Triad Sector, the language was proposed in 2814 by CDF higher-ups to make information breaches by the Coalition less effective.
    Phonetically, it sounds similar to Tau; but is almost incomprehensible to Tau speakers because of its extremely different structure. Very few words between Triadian and Tau are mutually shared.
    Nowadays, it is one of the official languages of the Triad Sector, spoken by the Triad Sector Government, TFA officials, and the TDF.

trait-language-no-natural-language-name = No Natural Language
trait-language-no-natural-language-desc = You cannot speak the language of your species' culture. You either grew up outside its culture, or never learned it due to some circumstances.

trait-language-Hydraspeak-name = Understand Hy'drav'tha
trait-language-Hydraspeak-desc =
    The spoken tongue of the Hydrakin, while impossible to speak without their unique vocal structure, is understandable to those that practice learning its odd nature of multiple meanings.
    The attentive ear can pick up on these differences, letting those that spend the time to learn it understand Hydrakin without need of a translator.

trait-language-RootSpeak-name = Understand Rootspeak
trait-language-RootSpeak-desc =
    "Spoken" by Diona, made up of creaks and rustling noises, Rootspeak is learnable with practice and persistence, if a bit harsh on the ear.
    While unable to be properly spoken without being a Diona, it is possible to understand them, albeit at the cost of playfully being called a small orange creature from a story book.

trait-language-Birdsong-name = Understand Birdsong
trait-language-Birdsong-desc =
    To the musically inclined, the emotion of music is as understandable as any spoken word, making learning and understanding the language of the Harpies trivial.
    Derived from the unqiue capabilities of their vocal cords, it is impossible to replicate by non-Harpies, but it is understandable to those who take the time to learn it, allowing for easier communication.
